{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning, doctor. Baby Naidoo, ten days old. I weighed him just now, 3.2 kilograms.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ta, sister. Send them in.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Sorry, hey, the robot on Voortrekker was out. I couldn't hear myself think with all the hooters behind the bakkie.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ag, that corner is a mess. Did you catch the Proteas last night?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ja, radio on the whole way. That catch at mid-off, I was yelling at the windscreen like a proper fool.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Then the storm sat over the ground and they stopped play for ages. Typical December, rain one minute and baking the next.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): And the tar was steaming afterwards. Lekker if you're not stuck in it. Anyway, shame, here he is.",
  "[SEG0008] person_4 (PATIENT): Eh.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): So. What's worrying you about him today?",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He's gone all yellow, doctor. Like someone rubbed turmeric all over him. It started, umm, I don't know, doctor, maybe day three, maybe day four.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): Is the yellow in the eyes as well, or just the skin?",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The eyes are proper yellow too. And when I pick him up he's like a wet rag, all...",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sleepy, or actually floppy in the arms and legs?",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Sleepy, ja. He only wants a feed every four hours, that's the other thing.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): Every four hours since when?",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (NURSE): Sorry, his little sock is off. Mom, want me to pop it back on?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ja, thanks. um, since about day two. Breast first, then about 40 ml of Lactogen on top.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any fever? And any vomiting?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No fever, and he hasn't vomited at all.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any allergies? Medicines, milk, anything at all?",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No, nothing like that. He's only ten days, we haven't come across anything.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Oh, and the clinic gave us vidamin D drops. One drop in his mouth every day, we've been doing that.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right, keep that going, it's just the vitamin. Yellow down over the chest and tummy, and the whites of the eyes are yellow. Fontanelle is soft and not sunken. Tummy's soft and the liver isn't big.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Is that bad, the yellow? My gogo says put him in the sun, but I wasn't sure, I...",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): Don't put him in the sun, hey, newborn skin burns. I'm thinking, uh, this is most likely physiological jaundice, just the liver catching up. At ten days I can't fully set aside breast-milk jaundice either.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): So what do we actually...",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (DOCTOR): Bloods today. Sister takes a serum bilirubin this morning, after this feed, and he doesn't need to fast for it.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (NURSE): Ja, I'll do it in the side room before you leave. This morning still.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (DOCTOR): If that number is borderline, we do a split bilirubin, the conjugated part. Not as a routine, only if it's sitting on the line.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): And if the yellow just doesn't come right?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (DOCTOR): If it does not settle, I'll send him for an abdominal sonar. Otherwise I'll see you back here on Friday, in three days, and we look at the result together.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Friday, ja. err, must I carry on with feeds every four hours? I've just been guessing, hey.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): Offer the breast about every three hours if he'll take it, keep the Lactogen top-up around 40 ml, and wake him if he's too sleepy to ask.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ok. Around 40 ml. I can do that.",
  "[SEG0035] person_4 (PATIENT): Mmm.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Funny, he slept straight through those hooters on the drive.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ja, they do that. Off you go with sister for the bloods, and I'll see you Friday.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Thanks, doctor. Come, boy."
 ],
